      ],
      "source": "https://indyencyclopedia.org/fairview-park/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early attractions included “King and Queen, the diving horses,” a pony track, canoeing, and a bandshell that drew visitors from the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://indyencyclopedia.org/fairview-park/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1903 the park added electric-powered rides, fountains, moving pictures, and a miniature railway, making it a pioneer of amusement technology.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://indyencyclopedia.org/fairview-park/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
